---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Meet Justin — JustinCredibleTech is the long-form companion to @JCredibleTech: consumer tech, space, science, Tesla/SpaceX/xAI/Starlink/EV."
>
  <div class="container about"><header class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">About</span><h1>About JustinCredibleTech</h1><p>Long-form companion to <strong>@JCredibleTech</strong>, for when a post needs room to breathe.</p></header><article class="prose">
    <p>
      Hey — I’m <strong>Justin</strong>. Online you’ll usually see me as
      <a href="https://x.com/JCredibleTech" rel="noopener noreferrer">@JCredibleTech</a>.
      Short posts are great for the “wait, what just shipped?” moments. This site is for the
      follow-up: context, timelines, and the “why should I care?” without the fluff.
    </p>

    <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
    <p>
      JustinCredibleTech covers the beat I already chase in socials — consumer tech drops,
      spaceflight milestones, and science that actually touches technology. Think new phones and
      foldables, lunar AI models, Starlink coverage leaps, EV and robotaxi reality checks, and the
      companies that keep showing up in that orbit: <strong>Tesla, SpaceX, xAI, Starlink</strong>,
      and the broader EV / space / AI stack.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Consumer tech</strong> — launches, specs that matter, and what “available Friday” really means.</li>
      <li><strong>Space</strong> — missions, maps, and orbital internet that changes who gets a signal.</li>
      <li><strong>Science × tech</strong> — open models, ice prospectivity, sensors, and tools researchers can actually download.</li>
      <li><strong>Mobility &amp; energy</strong> — EVs, autonomy, and the infrastructure that makes the demos stick.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Stay in the loop</h2>
    <p>
      Short takes land on
      <a href="https://x.com/JCredibleTech" rel="noopener noreferrer">@JCredibleTech</a>.
      Longer reads live here. If you want both, follow there and bookmark this site — or start with the
      <a href={withBase("blog/")}>latest posts</a> and grab the
      <a href={withBase("rss.xml")}>RSS feed</a> for your own schedule.
    </p>
    <p>
      Glad you’re here.
    </p>
  </article></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.about .prose{max-width:700px;margin-top:2rem}</style>
